**Superseded — archiving (janitor hygiene pass, run 0048).**

The obstruction proved here for *support-separated* adaptations is the special case of the piece-free necessity theorem recorded in `I-0327`: the same partition of unity on each pinned chart, applied to the union of the chart's piece traces rather than to one overlap, gives `DivisorAdaptation.isClosed_supportLocus_inter_chart_of_forall_noLeak` (`Picard/DivSchemeCertZarChartTrace.lean`, commit `49866bdd1`). `I-0327` also supplies the positive replacement this item lacked (swallow-or-miss, `Picard/DivSchemeCertZarSwallow.lean`, commit `206967379`), so its operational rule — "do not attack the certificate by choosing a cleverer adaptation" — is now refined rather than binding: one *does* choose the adaptation, but a swallow-or-miss one, and the obligation moves to chart design.

Nothing is lost by archiving:

- the second no-go this item alone recorded (the $L$-spanning $\iff$ flatness equivalence, `DivSchemeHighWindowSyzygy.lean:298`) has been copied onto `I-0327` as a comment;
- the Lean statements are unchanged in `Picard/DivSchemeCertZarSep.lean`;
- the durable record is roadmap leaf `AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.sep-nogo` (done), whose summary cites this item — archived items stay retrievable, so that citation still resolves.
EOF
)" 2>&1 | tail -2 && "$HORIZON_BIN" inbox archive I-0323 2>&1 | grep -E "archived|⚠|Error" | head -5

